  "interpretation": {
    "lineRecall": "Reference lines matched to a hypothesis line at or above matchThreshold, over reference lines. Low values mean lyrics are missing.",
    "linePrecision": "Matched hypothesis lines over all hypothesis lines. Falls when the pipeline invents extra rows.",
    "normalizedCharacterErrorRate": "Character edits over the whole joined document divided by reference characters; same normalization as tool/asr_transcript_eval.dart, so the numbers are comparable between the two tools.",
    "normalizedWordErrorRate": "Word edits (substitutions + insertions + deletions) over reference words, after the same normalization as the CER. Latin text is split into words; Han, kana and Hangul are one token per character, so for Chinese and Japanese this equals the character error rate.",
    "secondaryOnlyPrecision": "Of the rows the fused document marked as heard only by the secondary engine, the share that match a reference line. The rest are harmonies, ad-libs or noise the reviewer has to reject.",
    "secondaryRetention.retentionRate": "Reference lines found by the secondary engine but not the primary, that are still present in the fused document. Below 1.0 means fusion silently dropped a correct line.",
    "duplicateLineRate": "Extra hypothesis lines that restate another line within duplicateWindowMs, over hypothesis lines. Chorus repeats further apart are not counted. This is the metric that exposes the dual-engine fusion defect.",
    "startTimeMaeMs": "Mean absolute error of line start times over matched pairs, in milliseconds. Requires timestamps on both sides.",
    "within500msRate": "Share of matched pairs whose start times are within 500 ms.",
    "lineCountRatio": "Hypothesis lines over reference lines. 1.0 is ideal; above 1.2 means the pipeline is inserting rows.",
    "limitations": "Judges text, line segmentation, and timestamps only. Audio quality, vocal separation, and engine speed are out of scope."
